# gvsoc Snitch model, host-speed only: no simulated cycle changes (every ROI identical, traced runs
# byte-identical). After the RedMulE model was vectorised, gdb sampling of gvsoc_launcher showed the
# host time of the SoftHier platform inside the Snitch core model, on the path every offloaded FP
# instruction takes (integer core -> FPU sequencer -> FP subsystem -> response):
#   37 %  by-value copies of iss_insn_t (~900 B, with eight std::string arg names + a vector):
#         up to 12 per FP instruction (Iss::handle_req 3x, sequencer::req / gen_entry / write_entry /
#         read_entry / offload_event 6x, FP-ss handle_notif / get_latency / handle_event / acc_rsp 5x)
#   32 %  snitch_fp_ss.cpp formatted the full instruction trace with sprintf for every instruction
#         (iss_trace_save_args + iss_trace_dump) and then dropped it because no trace was active
#    5 %  up to 26 strstr() on the decoder label per instruction (decode.cpp int_/fp_offload_exec on
#         *every* integer instruction, snitch.cpp handle_result, snitch_fp_ss.cpp get_latency)
# Changes (all marked [SoftHier-fast]):
#   types.hpp      iss_insn_arg_t::name is a const char* (interned CSR name, iss_csr_name_cstr in
#                  csr.cpp; it is only set by csr_decode and only read by the trace dump); new
#                  iss_insn_t::label_class + iss_insn_label_class(): the original strstr predicates
#                  evaluated once per decoded instruction (decode.cpp decode_insn) and cached
#   insn_cache.hpp / decode.cpp   defined start values for name / label_class; cached label checks
#   snitch.cpp     handle_req copies the instruction once straight into acc_req; handle_result reads
#                  the response instruction through a pointer
#   OffloadRsp.hpp insn is a pointer into the FP subsystem's copy (the integer core only reads it
#                  synchronously inside the acc_rsp sync)
#   snitch_fp_ss.cpp  one copy into acc_req.insn and all work on it (get_latency by reference);
#                  iss_trace_save_args / iss_trace_dump only when trace.insn_trace.get_active()
#                  (constant false in the optim build, exactly as the integer core's
#                  iss_exec_insn_with_trace already does)
#   sequencer.cpp  entries are generated in place in the ring buffer and read into acc_req: one
#                  copy in, one copy out; the stagger register-index update for the trace is applied
#                  to the outgoing copy as before, the ring buffer entry is untouched as before
# The three libraries (integer core gen_isa_snitch_rv32imfdva_cpp_60335333, FP subsystem
# gen_isa_snitch_fp_ss_rv32imfdva_cpp_61161152, pulp/snitch/sequencer) share the iss_insn_t /
# OffloadReq / OffloadRsp layout and must be rebuilt together: install/models_fast/ (+ debug/) holds
# the set built from the patched sources (fp-ss pending fix, zfh flh/fsh, nseq ISA tables) with
# softhier-mlir/tools/iss_fast/gen_makefile.py; softhier_mlir/sim/gvsoc.py searches models_fast
# before models_fix and models (SOFTHIER_STOCK_MODELS=1 disables both).
# Measured 2026-10-08 (softhier-mlir docs/SIMULATOR_NOTES.md "Host speed of the Snitch ISS"):
#   run (tests/gvsoc/run.py)                 ROI ns (before = after)   wall s before -> after
#   gemm 1024x3072x768:256,256,256,1,0,all   520521                    47.6 -> 14.0
#   rowops --rows 256 --cols 768 --cluster all  508504                 16.8 -> 10.2
#   siglip-mlir --seq 256 --cluster all      4782253                   106.9 -> 28.1
#   attention --cluster 0                    26819562                  56.7 -> 8.1
#   mlir examples/siglip_encoder_layer.mlir  17851422                  424.7 -> 174.5
#   (same host load for both columns; CPU time 1.7-2.9x lower; traced debug run byte-identical
#   over the first 300 MB / 1.45 M lines of pe0 + fp_ss0 instruction dumps)
# Apply in /app/install/softhier (paths relative to the checkout) on top of gvsoc_snitch_fp_ss_pending.patch:
#   patch -p0 < gvsoc_iss_host_speed.patch
